1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,945
Cryptography hides in source, dependencies, configuration,

2
00:00:04,945 --> 00:00:07,911
certificates and container images.

3
00:00:07,911 --> 00:00:10,527
CryptoDrishti finds all of it

4
00:00:10,527 --> 00:00:14,543
— and turns it into one inventory you can defend.

5
00:00:15,293 --> 00:00:21,016
One scan: 23 distinct assets, 16 quantum-vulnerable

6
00:00:21,016 --> 00:00:26,643
— and the scan's own completeness stated up front.

7
00:00:27,393 --> 00:00:32,495
Five RSA findings in one scan. A signing call goes to ML-DSA-65.

8
00:00:32,495 --> 00:00:37,597
RSA wrapping a key is key establishment — a hybrid key exchange,

9
00:00:37,597 --> 00:00:40,514
a completely different migration.

10
00:00:40,514 --> 00:00:43,784
And a cipher list that never says what

11
00:00:43,784 --> 00:00:46,701
RSA is for gets no target at all.

12
00:00:46,701 --> 00:00:49,407
Purpose decides the migration.

13
00:00:50,157 --> 00:00:55,552
Open any finding and the chain is there: call site, symbol,

14
00:00:55,552 --> 00:01:01,507
technique, evidence strength, and the arithmetic behind the score.

15
00:01:02,257 --> 00:01:07,577
The output is a CycloneDX bill of materials,

16
00:01:07,577 --> 00:01:13,607
validated offline against the official JSON Schema.

17
00:01:14,357 --> 00:01:25,707
CryptoDrishti · Team Zero-Day · SIH26164
